\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{An unfixed rotation at a site}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{Permuting three basis vectors can carry the first vector to the
second in two ways. Both choices produce the same scalar. A link
entering that site may acquire different group elements when
expressed in those two frames. Which part of the entire reduced
connection can an invariant observable distinguish?}
